<Project Sdk="Microsoft.NET.Sdk">

  <PropertyGroup>
    <TargetFramework>net10.0</TargetFramework>
    <ImplicitUsings>enable</ImplicitUsings>
    <Nullable>enable</Nullable>
    <InvariantGlobalization>true</InvariantGlobalization>
  </PropertyGroup>

  <ItemGroup>
    <!-- BIO-RPT-003 owns api/features/bio-rpt-003/** only. No ProjectReference to Biolog.Api.csproj
         (one-way dependency, scripts/check-module-project-references.sh) and no ProjectReference to
         any other feature either, despite this story's real job being a READ-ONLY fan-in over
         several already-accepted sibling features' own audit sinks (BIO-IDN-006/Rbac,
         BIO-CRD-008/CardTemplates, BIO-RPT-002/ReportBuilder, BIO-CRD-007/CardProduction). That
         fan-in is composed entirely inside api/Biolog.Api/Modules/BioRpt003Module.cs (the one place
         in this codebase allowed to see every feature at once), through this project's own narrow
         Domain/IAuditEventSource.cs abstraction - the same shape every prior cross-story dependency
         in this epic uses (BIO-CRD-007's ICardIssueGateway, BIO-CRD-008's ISignatureAssetGateway).

         "Dependencies: BIO-ARC-003, BIO-IDN-006" in the approved story is build-wave GATING (what
         must already exist before this story can start) - both are satisfied (ADR-0003 is Accepted;
         Rbac/BIO-IDN-006 is fully built). The module's own DependsOn additionally names
         CardTemplates/ReportBuilder/CardProduction: real, honest DI-graph edges for already-
         accepted, earlier-wave features whose own audit sinks already expose a read helper
         explicitly commented "exposed for tests and a future audit-read endpoint" (see
         InMemoryProductionAuditSink.Events, InMemoryReportAuditSink.EventsForTenant) - this story IS
         that future endpoint. Zero edits to any of their owned files. See docs/features/bio-rpt-003/
         README.md "Which sources are wired, and why" for the full reasoning, disclosed rather than
         silently assumed.

         Namespace root is "AuditInvestigation". No new ADR-0001 canonical identifier is minted for
         a searched record itself - every NormalizedAuditRecord reuses its SOURCE feature's own
         evt_ event id verbatim (the whole point of ADR-0003's one envelope shape is that "everything
         that touched this tenant" is a single query over identically-shaped records, not a second
         id scheme layered on top). This project mints evt_ ids only for its OWN meta-audit trail
         (the export action itself, AC03's "audited"). -->
  </ItemGroup>

  <ItemGroup>
    <FrameworkReference Include="Microsoft.AspNetCore.App" />
  </ItemGroup>

  <ItemGroup>
    <InternalsVisibleTo Include="Biolog.Api" />
    <InternalsVisibleTo Include="Biolog.Features.AuditInvestigation.Tests" />
  </ItemGroup>

</Project>
